  data: {
    LLM: "For Beginners\n1. Save Your 8s: Keep 8s for emergencies when you cannot match the discard pile\n2. Change Suits Wisely: When playing an 8, choose a suit you have multiple cards of\n3. Force Draws: Play 2s strategically to make opponents draw cards\n4. Pay Attention: Watch what cards other players are picking up to deduce their hands\n5. Suit Management: Try to reduce the number of different suits in your hand\n\nCard Counting: Keep track of which 8s have been played\nSuit Control: Change suits to ones you know opponents don't have\nTiming Reverses: Use Aces to give yourself multiple turns in 2-player games\nSkip Chains: Coordinate Queens to skip dangerous opponents\n\nBluffing with 8s: Play an 8 early to mislead opponents about your hand composition\nDraw Pile Management: Control when opponents are forced to draw\nEndgame Planning: Plan your final cards to ensure you can play out\nOpponent Reading: Deduce opponent hand strength from their play patterns\n--",
